<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>KratosForge</displayName>
  <description>KratosForge policy settings</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="KratosForge">KratosForge</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_KratosForge">Not read by any current KratosForge build</string>
      <string id="cat_signin">Sign-in and updates</string>
      <string id="cat_fabric">Fabric, data and privacy</string>
      <string id="cat_notebooks">Notebooks</string>
      <string id="cat_packages">Packages</string>
      <string id="cat_sql">SQL and Warehouse</string>
      <string id="cat_integrations">AI tools and editors</string>
      <string id="cat_appstudio">App Studio</string>
      <string id="cat_appearance">Appearance and guidance</string>
      <string id="client_id">Client id</string>
      <string id="client_id_Help">The Microsoft Entra app (client) ID the app signs in with, for an organization that uses its own app registration. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: client_id. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="channel">Channel</string>
      <string id="channel_Help">Which release the app updates to: stable or preview. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: channel. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="channel_stable">stable</string>
      <string id="channel_preview">preview</string>
      <string id="show_preview">Show preview</string>
      <string id="show_preview_Help">Whether features still in preview are shown. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: show_preview. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="support_url">Support url</string>
      <string id="support_url_Help">Where Report a problem goes: an https link or a mailto: address. Policy file key: support_url. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="kernel_process">Kernel process</string>
      <string id="kernel_process_Help">Whether each notebook's cells run in a Python process of their own. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: kernel_process. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="auto_update">Auto update</string>
      <string id="auto_update_Help">False stops the app updating itself; IT then rolls out new builds. Policy file key: auto_update. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_fabric_runs">Allow fabric runs</string>
      <string id="allow_fabric_runs_Help">False stops the app starting jobs on Fabric capacity; work stays on the PC. Policy file key: allow_fabric_runs. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_replay_samples">Allow replay samples</string>
      <string id="allow_replay_samples_Help">False removes the sample of input data from replay bundles, so a bundle never holds lakehouse data. Policy file key: allow_replay_samples. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allowed_tenants">Allowed tenants</string>
      <string id="allowed_tenants_Help">Microsoft Entra tenant IDs people may sign in to. Any other account is signed out again. Add one item per line. Policy file key: allowed_tenants. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="local_retention_days">Local retention days</string>
      <string id="local_retention_days_Help">Days unused before local copies of lakehouse data are deleted; 0 keeps them. Policy file key: local_retention_days. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="telemetry">Telemetry</string>
      <string id="telemetry_Help">Whether daily usage counts are sent. Off unless turned on. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: telemetry. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="telemetry_connection_string">Telemetry connection string</string>
      <string id="telemetry_connection_string_Help">An Application Insights connection string, so usage data goes to the organization's own Azure Monitor. Policy file key: telemetry_connection_string. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="cell_time_limit_minutes">Cell time limit minutes</string>
      <string id="cell_time_limit_minutes_Help">Minutes a cell may run before it's interrupted; 0 for no limit. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: cell_time_limit_minutes. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="kernel_memory_limit_gb">Kernel memory limit gb</string>
      <string id="kernel_memory_limit_gb_Help">Gigabytes a notebook's process may use before it's ended; 0 for no limit. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: kernel_memory_limit_gb. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="kernel_max_sessions">Kernel max sessions</string>
      <string id="kernel_max_sessions_Help">How many notebooks keep a process of their own. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: kernel_max_sessions. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="kernel_idle_minutes">Kernel idle minutes</string>
      <string id="kernel_idle_minutes_Help">Idle minutes before a notebook's process is stopped; 0 keeps it. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: kernel_idle_minutes. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_optimize_lakehouse">Allow optimize lakehouse</string>
      <string id="allow_optimize_lakehouse_Help">False stops Optimize creating, connecting to or writing to a shared optimization lakehouse. Policy file key: allow_optimize_lakehouse. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_notebook_packages">Allow notebook packages</string>
      <string id="allow_notebook_packages_Help">False stops people installing packages into notebook environments. Policy file key: allow_notebook_packages. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="forge_animations">Forge animations</string>
      <string id="forge_animations_Help">The first motion switch: false means motion level 0 unless motion_level is set. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: forge_animations. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_staging_cleanup">Allow staging cleanup</string>
      <string id="allow_staging_cleanup_Help">False stops the Estate X-ray deleting leftover Dataflow Gen2 staging lakehouses; it still lists them. Policy file key: allow_staging_cleanup. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_page_rows">Sql page rows</string>
      <string id="sql_page_rows_Help">Rows on each page of a SQL result. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_page_rows. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_time_limit_minutes">Sql time limit minutes</string>
      <string id="sql_time_limit_minutes_Help">Minutes a SQL query may run before it's stopped; 0 for no limit. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_time_limit_minutes. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_memory_limit_percent">Sql memory limit percent</string>
      <string id="sql_memory_limit_percent_Help">Share of the PC's memory one SQL query may use. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_memory_limit_percent. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_max_concurrent">Sql max concurrent</string>
      <string id="sql_max_concurrent_Help">SQL queries that run at once; more wait in a queue. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_max_concurrent. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_temp_dir">Sql temp dir</string>
      <string id="sql_temp_dir_Help">Folder for spilled SQL data and result snapshots. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_temp_dir. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_result_retention_hours">Sql result retention hours</string>
      <string id="sql_result_retention_hours_Help">Hours a finished query's result is kept; 0 keeps it only until the app closes. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_result_retention_hours. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="sql_warehouse_writes">Sql warehouse writes</string>
      <string id="sql_warehouse_writes_Help">False refuses every change to a warehouse, so the Warehouse page only reads. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: sql_warehouse_writes. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="wh_monitoring_views">Wh monitoring views</string>
      <string id="wh_monitoring_views_Help">False stops the app creating monitoring views in Fabric. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: wh_monitoring_views. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="wh_monitoring_auto">Wh monitoring auto</string>
      <string id="wh_monitoring_auto_Help">Workspace IDs whose warehouses get monitoring views without asking again. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Add one item per line. Policy file key: wh_monitoring_auto. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_level">Motion level</string>
      <string id="motion_level_Help">Visual intensity: 0 Off, 1 Minimal, 2 Refined, 3 Expressive. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_level. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_wolf">Motion wolf</string>
      <string id="motion_wolf_Help">Whether the wolf effects show at motion levels 2 and 3. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_wolf. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_sparks">Motion sparks</string>
      <string id="motion_sparks_Help">Whether spark effects show at motion levels 2 and 3. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_sparks. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_achievements">Motion achievements</string>
      <string id="motion_achievements_Help">Whether achievement celebrations show at motion levels 2 and 3. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_achievements. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_ambient">Motion ambient</string>
      <string id="motion_ambient_Help">Whether ambient effects show at motion levels 2 and 3. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_ambient. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="motion_follow_system">Motion follow system</string>
      <string id="motion_follow_system_Help">Whether Windows' reduced-motion setting turns decorative motion off. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: motion_follow_system. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_signed_out_schedules">Allow signed out schedules</string>
      <string id="allow_signed_out_schedules_Help">False stops people setting schedules on this PC to run while they're signed out of Windows. Policy file key: allow_signed_out_schedules. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="platform_presence">Platform presence</string>
      <string id="platform_presence_Help">True records owners' last-used dates in the platform catalog, which everyone who reads the catalog sees. Policy file key: platform_presence. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="onelake_writes">Onelake writes</string>
      <string id="onelake_writes_Help">local_first stages a notebook's table writes on the PC and uploads them in the background; direct writes each one to OneLake before the next line runs. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: onelake_writes. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="onelake_writes_local_first">local_first</string>
      <string id="onelake_writes_direct">direct</string>
      <string id="onelake_compression">Onelake compression</string>
      <string id="onelake_compression_Help">The Parquet codec for tables written to OneLake: zstd or snappy. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: onelake_compression. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="onelake_compression_zstd">zstd</string>
      <string id="onelake_compression_snappy">snappy</string>
      <string id="onelake_skip_unchanged">Onelake skip unchanged</string>
      <string id="onelake_skip_unchanged_Help">Whether an overwrite whose rows match what the app last wrote uploads nothing. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: onelake_skip_unchanged. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="wh_open_in">Wh open in</string>
      <string id="wh_open_in_Help">What opening a warehouse by its name does: the Warehouse page (kratosforge) or Fabric's editor (fabric). People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: wh_open_in. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="wh_open_in_kratosforge">kratosforge</string>
      <string id="wh_open_in_fabric">fabric</string>
      <string id="fabric_full_screen">Fabric full screen</string>
      <string id="fabric_full_screen_Help">Whether the Fabric portal tab fills the window. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: fabric_full_screen. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_explanations">Ui explanations</string>
      <string id="ui_explanations_Help">Whether each page's explanation shows beside it or opens on request. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: ui_explanations. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_explanations_beside">beside</string>
      <string id="ui_explanations_on_request">on_request</string>
      <string id="ui_preview_marks">Ui preview marks</string>
      <string id="ui_preview_marks_Help">How Preview features are marked: tags or dots. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: ui_preview_marks. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_preview_marks_tags">tags</string>
      <string id="ui_preview_marks_dots">dots</string>
      <string id="ui_density">Ui density</string>
      <string id="ui_density_Help">Spacing in tables, lists and toolbars: comfortable or compact. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: ui_density. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_density_comfortable">comfortable</string>
      <string id="ui_density_compact">compact</string>
      <string id="ui_skin">Ui skin</string>
      <string id="ui_skin_Help">The platform skin's ID. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: ui_skin. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_color_mode">Ui color mode</string>
      <string id="ui_color_mode_Help">skin follows the skin's own color mode; light or dark overrides it. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: ui_color_mode. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="ui_color_mode_skin">skin</string>
      <string id="ui_color_mode_light">light</string>
      <string id="ui_color_mode_dark">dark</string>
      <string id="learn_mode">Learn mode</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_Help">How much learning guidance shows beside work: expert, professional or guided. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: learn_mode. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_expert">expert</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_professional">professional</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_guided">guided</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql">Learn mode sql</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql_Help">The guidance level for SQL findings only; same follows learn_mode. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: learn_mode_sql. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql_same">same</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql_expert">expert</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql_professional">professional</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_sql_guided">guided</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks">Learn mode notebooks</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks_Help">The guidance level for notebook findings only; same follows learn_mode. People can also change it in Settings; this policy fixes it. Policy file key: learn_mode_notebooks. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks_same">same</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks_expert">expert</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks_professional">professional</string>
      <string id="learn_mode_notebooks_guided">guided</string>
      <string id="notebook_package_folder">Notebook package folder</string>
      <string id="notebook_package_folder_Help">A folder of approved .whl files that notebook environments install from first. Policy file key: notebook_package_folder. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_pypi_packages">Allow pypi packages</string>
      <string id="allow_pypi_packages_Help">False stops notebook environments reaching PyPI for a package the folder doesn't have. Policy file key: allow_pypi_packages. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="allow_dbconnect_install">Allow dbconnect install</string>
      <string id="allow_dbconnect_install_Help">False stops the app installing the Databricks Connect client. Policy file key: allow_dbconnect_install. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="dbconnect_index_url">Dbconnect index url</string>
      <string id="dbconnect_index_url_Help">The package index the Databricks Connect client is fetched from, for networks that mirror PyPI. Policy file key: dbconnect_index_url. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="integrations">Integrations</string>
      <string id="integrations_Help">False turns external AI tools off on this PC. Policy file key: integrations. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="integrations_max_permissions">Integrations max permissions</string>
      <string id="integrations_max_permissions_Help">The permission categories an external tool may be given. Add one item per line. Policy file key: integrations_max_permissions. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="integrations_http">Integrations http</string>
      <string id="integrations_http_Help">False stops the local HTTP API being switched on. Policy file key: integrations_http. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="integrations_extensions">Integrations extensions</string>
      <string id="integrations_extensions_Help">The extensions the person may turn on, by ID. Add one item per line. Policy file key: integrations_extensions. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="integrations_editors">Integrations editors</string>
      <string id="integrations_editors_Help">False stops editors such as VS Code being paired to run notebooks. Policy file key: integrations_editors. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="receipt_redactions">Receipt redactions</string>
      <string id="receipt_redactions_Help">Parts of a receipt every export leaves out. Add one item per line. Policy file key: receipt_redactions. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="appstudio_models">Appstudio models</string>
      <string id="appstudio_models_Help">False stops App Studio using, adding or testing a model connection. Policy file key: appstudio_models. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="appstudio_providers">Appstudio providers</string>
      <string id="appstudio_providers_Help">The model providers a connection may use, by ID. Add one item per line. Policy file key: appstudio_providers. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="appstudio_hosts">Appstudio hosts</string>
      <string id="appstudio_hosts_Help">Exact host names an Azure OpenAI or OpenAI-compatible connection may use. Add one item per line. Policy file key: appstudio_hosts. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="appstudio_sample_rows">Appstudio sample rows</string>
      <string id="appstudio_sample_rows_Help">False stops any connection sending sample rows. Policy file key: appstudio_sample_rows. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="fabric_view_sign_in_hosts">Fabric view sign in hosts</string>
      <string id="fabric_view_sign_in_hosts_Help">Exact host names of the organization's own identity provider (AD FS, Okta, Ping) that the Fabric view may open during sign-in. Add one item per line. Policy file key: fabric_view_sign_in_hosts. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="register_link_scheme">Register link scheme</string>
      <string id="register_link_scheme_Help">False stops the app registering kratosforge:// links for the Windows user, and removes a registration it made. Policy file key: register_link_scheme. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
      <string id="engine_download_url">Engine download url</string>
      <string id="engine_download_url_Help">An https folder the app downloads its engine from instead of GitHub, with auto_update false. Read by the app itself; trusted only when the policy file is admin-only. Policy file key: engine_download_url. No current KratosForge build reads this policy from the registry. Until the release notes say registry policy is supported, set it in %ProgramData%\FabricDesktop\policy.json instead.</string>
    </stringTable>
